import random

class InvestmentBot:
    def __init__(self):
        self.stocks = ["AAPL", "TSLA", "AMZN", "GOOG", "MSFT"]
        self.bonds = ["US Treasury", "Corporate Bonds", "Municipal Bonds", "CDs"]
        self.other_products = ["ETFs", "Mutual Funds", "Options", "Futures"]

    def recommend_stocks(self):
        return random.choice(self.stocks)

    def recommend_bonds(self):
        return random.choice(self.bonds)

    def recommend_other_products(self):
        return random.choice(self.other_products)

    def recommend_investments(self):
        stock = self.recommend_stocks()
        bond = self.recommend_bonds()
        other_product = self.recommend_other_products()

        return f"Recommended investments: {stock}, {bond}, {other_product}"

bot = InvestmentBot()
print(bot.recommend_investments())
```

In this bot, there are three lists of investment products: stocks, bonds, and other products. The bot randomly selects one item from each list and returns them as a recommendation. You can run the bot multiple times to get different recommendations. The bot can be expanded to include more investment products and to make more sophisticated recommendations based on market trends, historical performance, and user preferences. <|end|>
